WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.800
This is the public demo: fifty thousand tasks open in the browser, with bars, names and the critical path in red.

2
00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:16.588
Zoom from years down to days. Weekends shade in, and the view stays anchored under the cursor.

3
00:00:17.191 --> 00:00:22.611
Select a task and its driving path lights up, nearest predecessor first.

4
00:00:23.216 --> 00:00:27.396
Drag a critical task later, and the whole schedule re-solves as you move.

5
00:00:29.725 --> 00:00:35.795
Now scroll through all fifty thousand tasks, top to bottom. The slowest frame is in the caption.

6
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:43.950
Critical only hides every task that has float, so the longest path stands alone.

7
00:00:44.557 --> 00:00:49.887
Lookahead keeps only the activities in a three-week window, with their summaries.

8
00:00:50.495 --> 00:00:56.835
Open a Primavera P6 file. Its actual dates, progress and data date all apply.

9
00:01:02.099 --> 00:01:08.199
Filter by an activity code, here the trade Mechanical, to see one crew's work.

10
00:01:08.798 --> 00:01:16.738
Change a link's type and lag, from start to start plus eight days to finish to start plus two.

11
00:01:17.348 --> 00:01:22.338
Show moved keeps only the tasks that edit moved, so you can see what it cost.

12
00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:28.448
Rust, WebAssembly and the GPU, built as a component you can put in your own product.
